R"VG(
# account_herbal.vg (H-04; the second pass 2026-10-10): the account (the stores, the tithes, the herd: the people's own crops, vessels,
# measures and coin), the herbal (the plants about the place, each a name, where it grows, how it is made up and what for: the world's
# trees, rivers and hills, a word of the people's own now and then) and the inscription on a work finished.

# ---- the account: the stores, the tithes, the herd ------------------------------------------------------------------------

genre.account (words=15..87)
  {account.head} {account.items} {account.end}

account.head (formula)
  (2) The count of the stores of {$home}, {season.now} of the year {#year:digits}:
  The tithe of {$home} for the year {#year:digits}:
  Received at the granary of {$seat}:
  What is owed to {hall} by the houses of {$home}:
  The store-room of {holyplace}, as counted in {season.now}:
  Brought in to {$seat} from the villages, the year {#year:digits}:
  (contact=1) Traded with the {other} at {city2}, the year {#year:digits}:

account.items
  {account.item} {account.item} {account.item} {account.item}.
  {account.item} {account.item} {account.item}.
  {account.item} {account.item} {account.item} {account.item} {account.item}.

account.item
  (once) {nbig} {measure.load} of {crop};
  (once) {n} {vessel} of {crop2};
  (once) {n} {vessel} of {drink};
  (once) {nbig} {herd}, {n} of them lame;
  (once) {n} bolts of {colour.any} cloth;
  (once) salt, {n} {vessel};
  (once) {fuel}, enough for {season.next};
  (once) iron, {n} bars;
  (once) honey, {n} {vessel}, one broken;
  (once) seed for {season.next}, {n} {measure.load};
  (once) {n} days of work on {town.edge}, owed and not given;
  (once) {fruit}, {n} {measure.load}, half of them bruised;
  (once) {veg}, {n} {measure.load};
  (once) {material} for the roof of {hall}, {n} loads;
  (once) {#n} {coin} in coin, and {#n} that will not ring true;
  (once) {n} {vessel} of {food}, salted;
  (once coast=1|river=1) {fish}, dried, {n} {measure.load};
  (once) skins of the {game}, {n};
  (once) {n} {med.ac.made} from the {craft}-house;
  (once) for the lamps of {holyplace}, oil, {n} {vessel};
  (once contact=1) {n} skins from the {other}, for salt;
  (once contact=1) owed to the traders of the {other}, {#n} {coin};

med.ac.made
  pots
  baskets
  blankets
  pairs of shoes
  knives
  lengths of rope
  saddles

account.end (formula)
  (once harvest<=1) Less than last year, and last year was less than the year before.
  (once harvest>=3) More than the granary holds; the rest is in the hall.
  (once famine=1) Nothing to send to {$seat} this year. Let them come and count it themselves.
  Counted twice and found the same.
  Counted by the scribe of {$home}, and the seal set.
  (stage>=2) Counted, and there is no one to give it to.
  Counted {time.of}, by lamplight, so forgive the hand.
  Counted, and the {pest} have had their share already.

# ---- the herbal -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

genre.herbal (words=33..121)
  {herbal.open}\n{herbal.entry}\n{herbal.entry}\n{herbal.entry}

herbal.open (formula)
  Of the plants that grow about {$home}, and what they are good for.
  The herbal of {$home}, as the old women taught it.
  What grows round {$home}, and what to do with it, and what not.
  The plants of {land}, written down before they are forgotten.

herbal.entry
  (3 once) {med.hb.plant}: {med.hb.prep}, {med.hb.use}{med.hb.remark}
  (3 once) {med.hb.plant}: {med.hb.prep}, {med.hb.use}{med.hb.remark}
  (2 once) {med.hb.named}: {med.hb.prep}, {med.hb.use}{med.hb.remark}
  (once) {med.hb.odd}

med.hb.plant
  The {med.hb.adj} {med.hb.kind} that grows {med.hb.where}
  The {med.hb.kind} of {med.hb.place}
  The {med.hb.adj} {med.hb.kind}, which the {herd} will not eat
  The {med.hb.kind} with {colour.any} flowers that grows {med.hb.where}
  The {med.hb.adj} {med.hb.kind} of {mountain}

med.hb.named
  {~feverleaf}, the {med.hb.adj} {med.hb.kind} {med.hb.where}
  {~bonemend}, which grows {med.hb.where}
  {~sleepweed}, the low {med.hb.kind} with the {colour.any} root
  {~bitterbark}, from the {tree} {med.hb.where2}
  {~moonflower}, which opens at night {med.hb.where}

med.hb.adj
  bitter
  grey
  red
  white
  hairy
  creeping
  sweet
  stinking
  low
  tall
  spotted
  sticky
  pale
  thorny

med.hb.kind
  leaf
  moss
  root
  berry
  weed
  bark
  thistle
  nettle
  fern
  rush
  vine
  mushroom
  creeper
  sedge

med.hb.where
  under the {tree}
  by {river}
  on {mountain}
  in {land}
  by {watersrc}
  on the walls of {$home}
  in the shade of {holyplace}
  in the {crop} where nobody wants it
  on the graves at {deadplace}
  in the ruts of the road to {city2}
  where the {herd} have lain
med.hb.where2
  by {river}
  on {mountain}
  behind {holyplace}
med.hb.place
  the old fields
  the river bank
  the burnt ground
  the ditches
  the high pasture

med.hb.prep
  boiled
  steeped in {drink}
  pounded with honey
  dried and burnt, and the smoke breathed
  chewed raw
  laid on and bound
  mixed with {food}
  ground with salt
  pressed for its juice
  soaked overnight in {watersrc.n} water
  roasted in the ashes

med.hb.use
  for a fever
  for the cough, in {season.now}
  for wounds
  for sleep
  for the eyes, after {weather}
  for the teeth
  for women in labour
  for the {herd} when they will not eat
  against the {pest} in the store
  for the gripes
  for those who cannot stop talking
  for a sour stomach after {festival}
  for burns from the {craft}
  for the old, when their hands shake

med.hb.remark
  (3) .
  ; it stings, and that is how you know it works.
  ; the {herd} will not touch it, which tells you something.
  ; not to be given to children, or to the priest.
  ; my teacher swore by it, and died at ninety.
  ; it tastes of {med.hb.taste}, and there is no helping that.
  ; pick it before {festival}, or not at all.
  ; it does nothing, but the sick feel looked after.

med.hb.taste
  dust
  old shoes
  the inside of a {vessel.one.n}
  {crop2}
  regret

# the old women's warnings, one-liners (each people its own few)
med.hb.odd (share=0.5)
  The red berry of the hedges: not to be eaten. The birds eat it. We are not birds.
  The white mushroom of the old fields: never. Not even dried. Not even for an enemy.
  The flower that opens at night: for nothing at all, but it smells of {season.next}, and the sick like it by the bed.
  Salt and ash: for the teeth, though it does not taste like it.
  The grey moss of {mountain}: for wounds, laid on and bound; it stings, and that is how you know it works.
  The root of the river reed: for the cough, with honey.
  (desert=1) The thorn tree's gum: for the eyes, after the dust.
  The black seed that the {bird} leave alone: leave it alone.
  {crop2}, steeped: for sleep, and for those who cannot stop talking.

# ---- the inscription on a work finished --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

genre.inscription (words=13..53)
  {@event built inscription 6}

inscription.built
  {$e.work} was raised here {inscr.by}, in the {#$e.year:ord} year of {city}, after {#$e.value|year} of work. {inscr.end}
  This is {$e.work} of {$e.place}, {inscr.by}. {inscr.end}
  {inscr.by.cap}, {$e.work} of {walls.of}, finished in {season.now} of the year {#$e.year:digits}. {inscr.end}
  Here {$e.work} stands, {inscr.by}, {inscr.what}. {inscr.end}
  For {god} and for {$e.place}: {$e.work}, {#$e.value|year} in the building. {inscr.end}
inscription.none
  This stone was set here in the {#year:ord} year of {city}. {inscr.end}
  This stone was set here at {$home} under {ruler.the}. {inscr.end}

inscr.by
  (has:$e.a) the work of {$e.a:name}
  (has:$ruler) in the rule of {$ruler:full}
  (has:$ruler.epithet) in the rule of {$ruler:full} {$ruler.epithet}
  by the people of {$e.place}
  by the {med.chr.trades} of {$e.place}
inscr.by.cap
  (has:$e.a) Raised by {$e.a:name}
  By the hands of {$e.place}
  For {ruler.the}
inscr.what
  with {motif.over} cut over the door
  painted {colour.holy} where the sun strikes it
  of {walls.of} carried from {mountain}
  the {nth} of its kind in the land

inscr.end
  Let it stand {simile}.
  {god} keep it, and those who use it.
  Whoever breaks it, let the {crop} fail in their fields.
  Remember the ones who carried the stone.
  Whoever reads this, say the name of the one who made it.
  It was built to outlast us. Let it.
)VG"
